# A copy of a variable that may stay empty — refused

`tussen` is defined only when `pas_toe` holds. Catala reads a variable hard:
when `pas_toe` is false, `kopie equals tussen` raises "no applicable rule to
define this variable", while the IR leaves `kopie` empty and `kopie + 1`
reads that empty operand as 0. The plugin refuses the read of `tussen`.
Own-authored, rights-free.

```catala
declaration scope Aanslag:
  input pas_toe content boolean
  internal tussen content integer
  internal kopie content integer
  output heffing content integer

scope Aanslag:
  definition tussen under condition pas_toe consequence equals 5
  definition kopie equals tussen
  definition heffing equals kopie + 1
```
